     "counterpoint": "Remakes may not be a symptom of a squeeze at all: the evidence is about global trends and a spending drop, not a documented shift from Indian originals to remakes. India's biggest hits are still originals, and an adapted format can be a legitimate creative route, so the piece's causal link between budget cuts and remakes is inferred rather than proven. The piece should concede this and frame its claim as the most plausible reading of the pressures.",
